    "Tampered": "The sealed bytes changed after sealing.",
    "WrongBinding": "The certificate was sealed under the key of another salt.",
    "LowOrder": "One ephemeral has low order, so the shared secret is all zero. The other side MUST refuse before the AEAD: the responder seals nothing, and the requester never opens the forged sealed, which an attacker can produce under the zero secret."
